<title>FRANCE: French Q4 industrial production prices seen off in Q4.</title>
<headline>French Q4 industrial production prices seen off in Q4.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French producer prices are expected to fall slightly in the fourth quarter, although prices for semi-finished goods, consumer goods and those in the manufacturing industry are expected to rise a touch, national statistics institute INSEE said in its quarterly survey of industry.</p>
<p>It gave the following figures for output prices, by percentage change from previous quarter (seasonally adjusted unless stated)</p>
<p>					     Q496    Q396    Q296     Q495</p>
<p>Price change of pvs quarter (unadj) =	-0.4    -0.5     -0.4</p>
<p>  -- Manufacturing industry	   =	-0.6    -0.7     -0.5</p>
<p>  -- Semi-finished goods		=	-1.4    -1.1     -1.2</p>
<p>  -- Consumer goods		     =	-0.2    -0.4     -0.5</p>
<p>Price change expected next quarter-0.1     -0.2     0.0	0.1</p>
<p>  -- Manufacturing industry	  0.1     -0.2    -0.2	0.0</p>
<p>  -- Semi-finished goods	     0.1     -0.1    -0.6     -0.6</p>
<p>  -- Consumer goods		    0.1     -0.1     0.0	0.2</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5381</p>
</text>
